<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6693" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">captātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				reaching after</i> or <i>catching at
			something</i> (rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verborum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Part. Or. 23, 81</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puerilis vocum similium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 3, 57</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">testamenti,</span>”
				<i>legacy-hunting</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					20, 14, 57, § 160</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 6,
			51</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In fencing, t. t., <i>a feint</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 5,
				13, 54</span></i>.</div>
